; BOUNCE BONANZA - song 10, course 5 "Kite Hill": "Kite Hill" (SPEC.md 130.20)
;
; D major in 6/8 at 121 to the dotted quarter: a 16th is a row, and the rows
; alternate five and four sub-ticks (`groove 5 4`), so an 8th is always 9 and
; a bar of six 8ths is 54 sub-ticks, 0.99 s. A pattern is FOUR bars, 3.96 s.
; No other course song is in compound time (Windmill Lane is a 3/4 waltz).
;
; The course is wind carrying a ball up a hill, so the tune FLOATS and
; CLIMBS. Its MOTIF is a kite let out on its string and dipping back: up a
; broken chord in the 6/8's own long-short lilt, through the RAISED FOURTH
; (G#, the lydian's "air"), to the top, and down the chord again:
;   a4 >d8 f+4 g+8 | a4. f+4 d8                    (over D)
; and every phrase starts a step higher than the last - on A over D, on B
; over Em, on C# over F#m, on D over G (whose own raised fourth, C#, is in
; the key) - so the tops climb A, B, C#, D. The fifth phrase runs up an E7
; chord to an E that is HELD, a bar and a third: the THERMAL, the only long
; note in A, and the glide back down an A7.
;
; B is the GLIDE, and goes the other way: slow falling notes, two to a bar,
; over G D Em A7; then THE GUST - the song's one event, a quick run up six
; 16ths through the raised fourth that STOPS DEAD on a clipped note, the
; harp stopping with it - and a bar's BREATH with the harp alone before the
; tune climbs again. The second A reaches the SUMMIT (E G over A7, the F#6
; held, down to D) and the second B glides in running 8ths. Intro, A B A' B'
; for ever: the loop is 10 patterns, 40 bars, 39.5 s; the intro is the harp
; alone, the gust and the breath.
;
; Nothing here is a turning figure (Windmill Lane's) or a hop onto the beat
; (Little Hop's): every phrase of A is one arc, up and back, every phrase of
; B falls, and the accompaniment is one broken chord a bar that also rises -
; root, fifth, tenth, long-short-long.
;
; THE SPEAKER: the lead carries it, and `spkbass` gives the harp's broken
; chord to every rest of the lead: the two bars before the tune, the breath
; after each gust, and the half bar that ends each A. Only the kick blips
; (every two bars, on a phrase's first note; none under the gust or the
; thermal); the hats are the AdLib's. No arpeggio macro and no vibrato is
; written: a held note is one tone, and the song sends the speaker fewer
; tones a second than any other course's.
; ON THE ADLIB the recorder sings over the harp and a soft string pad whose
; chords all sit BELOW the tune (First Roll's lesson), and the chip's own
; vibrato is on the held notes.

song kitehill "Kite Hill"
groove 5 4
unit 16
rows 48
measure 12
spkbass
voice lead recorder
voice bass harp
voice chord strings

; --- the intro: the harp alone, then the gust and the breath, D D E7 A7 ---------
lead LI = r2. | r2. | v13 o5 q0 e16 f+16 g+16 a16 b16 >c+16 q5 d8 r4 | r2. |
bass BI = v13 o3 d4 a8 >f+4. | <d4 b8 >f+4. | <e4 b8 r4. | <a4 >g8 >c+4. |
chord CI = v10 o3 [a >d f+]2.^2. | [g+ b >d]2. | [g >c+ e]2. |

; --- A: the climb. Each phrase an arc a step higher; the tops A B C# D ----------
lead LA1 = v13 o4 a4 >d8 f+4 g+8 | a4. f+4 d8 | <b4 >e8 g4 a8 | b4. g4 e8 |
lead LA2 = v13 o5 c+4 f+8 a4 b8 | >c+4. <a4 f+8 | d4 g8 b4 >c+8 | d4. <b4 g8 |
; the thermal: up the E7 chord, the E held a bar and a third, the glide down A7
lead LA3 = v13 o5 e4 g+8 b4 >d8 | e2.&e4 c+8 <a4 g8 | f+4. r4. |
; the summit (the second A's): E G over A7, the F#6 held, down to D
lead LA4 = v13 o5 e4 g+8 b4 >d8 | e4. g4 e8 | f+2. | d4. r4. |
bass BA1 = v13 o3 d4 a8 >f+4. | <d4 a8 >f+4. | <e4 b8 >g4. | <e4 b8 >g4. |
bass BA2 = v13 o3 f+4 >c+8 a4. | <f+4 >c+8 a4. | <g4 >d8 b4. | <g4 >d8 b4. |
bass BA3 = v13 o3 e4 b8 >g+4. | <a4 >e8 >c+4. | <<<a4 >g8 >c+4. | <d4 a8 >f+4. |
bass BA4 = v13 o3 e4 b8 >g+4. | <<a4 >g8 >c+4. | <d4 a8 >f+4. | <d4 a8 >f+4. |
chord CA1 = v10 o3 [a >d f+]2.^2. | [g b >e]2.^2. |
chord CA2 = v10 o3 [a >c+ f+]2.^2. | [g b >d]2.^2. |
chord CA3 = v10 o3 [g+ b >d]2. | [a >c+ e]2. | [g >c+ e]2. | [a >d f+]2. |
chord CA4 = v10 o3 [g+ b >d]2. | [g >c+ e]2. | [a >d f+]2.^2. |

; --- B: the glide. Slow falling notes, G D Em A7, then the gust and the breath --
lead LB1 = v13 o6 d4. <b4. | a4. f+4. | g4. e4. | c+4 e8 a4. |
lead LB2 = v13 o6 e4 d8 <b4 g8 | f+4 a8 >d4. |
           q0 <e16 f+16 g+16 a16 b16 >c+16 q5 d8 r4 | r2. |
; the second B's first half: the same fall in running 8ths, up to G6 and E6
lead LB3 = v13 o6 d8 <b8 g8 b8 >d8 g8 | f+8 d8 <a8 f+8 a8 >d8 |
           e8 <b8 g8 e8 g8 b8 | a4 >c+8 e4. |
bass BB1 = v13 o3 g4 >d8 b4. | <d4 a8 >f+4. | <e4 b8 >g4. | <<a4 >g8 >c+4. |
bass BB2 = v13 o3 g4 >d8 b4. | <d4 a8 >f+4. | <e4 b8 r4. | <a4 >g8 >c+4. |
chord CB1 = v10 o3 [g b >d]2. | [a >d f+]2. | [g b >e]2. | [g >c+ e]2. |
chord CB2 = v10 o3 [g b >d]2. | [a >d f+]2. | [g+ b >d]2. | [g >c+ e]2. |

; the beat: a kick every two bars and the hats' long-short. The gust and the
; breath are bare (a kick there blipped over the run's first note on the
; speaker), and under the thermal the third bar has no kick, so the speaker
; holds the E unbroken
drum DA = k4 h8 h4 h8 | h4 h8 h4 h8 | k4 h8 h4 h8 | h4 h8 h4 h8 |
drum DB = k4 h8 h4 h8 | h4 h8 h4 h8 | r1. |
drum DT = k4 h8 h4 h8 | h4 h8 h4 h8 | h4 h8 h4 h8 | h4 h8 h4 h8 |

order LI  BI  CI  DB          ; 0: the intro, D D E7 A7
order LA1 BA1 CA1 DA          ; 1: A   D Em - the loop comes back here
order LA2 BA2 CA2 DA          ; 2:     F#m G
order LA3 BA3 CA3 DT          ; 3:     E7 A A7 D, the thermal
order LB1 BB1 CB1 DA          ; 4: B   G D Em A7
order LB2 BB2 CB2 DB          ; 5:     G D E7 A7, the gust and the breath
order LA1 BA1 CA1 DA          ; 6: A'  D Em
order LA2 BA2 CA2 DA          ; 7:     F#m G
order LA4 BA4 CA4 DA          ; 8:     E7 A7 D, the summit
order LB3 BB1 CB1 DA          ; 9: B'  G D Em A7, running
order LB2 BB2 CB2 DB          ; 10:    G D E7 A7, the gust and the breath
loop 1
